<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Nov housing finance falls 2.9 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Nov housing finance falls 2.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance commitments for owner-occupied housing in Australia fell 2.9 percent by volume to 38,460 dwellings in November from a downwardly revised 39,592 in October, seasonally-adjusted, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In value terms, housing finance fell to A$3.95 billion in November from A$3.97 billion in October, the bureau said.</p>
<p>Australian housing finance, November 1996 -</p>
<p>    Dwelling commitments	Nov 96     Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	 38,460     39,592     37,998</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		    38,737     41,022     40,489</p>
<p>    Trend			   40,194     40,158     38,240</p>
<p>Value (A$ billion)</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	  3.95	 3.97	  3.70</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		     3.98	 4.10	  3.90</p>
<p>    Trend estimates		4.08	 4.04	  4.00</p>
<p>The bureau said finance commitments for the construction of new dwellings fell 4.4 percent, in seasonally adjusted terms, to 5,413.</p>
<p>The number of dwellings refinanced fell 14.6 percent to 7,662 from 8,974 in October.</p>
<p>Excluding refinancing, commitments rose 0.6 percent.</p>
<p>The bureau said new seasonal adjustment factors as a result of the annual seasonal reanalysis were introduced this month.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
